PARITY — every web branch reproduced (web source is the spec)
  • mode: create (initial==null) vs edit (initial!=null) — title + key-immutability + disabled key field.
  • value editor: free-form JSON textarea; trimmed-empty => "Value is required."; bad JSON =>
    "Invalid JSON: {msg}"; else valid. Backend accepts ANY JSON value => parser is .fragmentsAllowed
    (bare true/42/"x" valid), exactly like browser JSON.parse.
  • edit seed = JSON.stringify(initial.value, null, 2) reproduced by FlagJSON.pretty (2-space, sorted keys).
  • canSave = parsed.ok && key.trim>0 && reason.trim>0 && !saving  (FlagEditValidator.canSave, web-faithful).
  • title: edit => 'Edit flag "{key}"' ; create => 'Create flag'. Footer Cancel + Save flag(loading=saving).
  • re-seed on open/initial change (web useEffect) => FlagEditModel reseed-on-seedToken.
  STATES (every one renders — no hidden surface; the web is a controlled form, so the loading/error/
  connectivity axes are SANCTIONED P4 leaf additions, documented in-code, mapped honestly to a WRITE
  surface — never fabricated):
    ready(create/edit form) · loading(edit-seed skeleton) · error(load failure + Retry) ·
    validation(value empty / invalid JSON / valid; key & reason required) · saving(spinner+disabled) ·
    save-error(inline retryable banner) · live / stale(Reload + 1x auto-refresh) / offline(Save gated + banner).
  i18n: web keys VERBATIM (admin.flags.drawer.*, admin.flags.editor.*, common.cancel) + native chrome
        keys (flagEdit.*). No English literals in Swift (every string via FlagEditStrings facade,
        Text(verbatim:)). Acceptance: every source key has a catalog entry — see FlagEditDrawer.strings.
  Telemetry: view.opened with surface slug "FlagEditDrawer" emitted once on presentation (P1/S11).
  a11y: every interactive control labelled; key field carries an "immutable" hint while editing;
        value field announces its parse error; Dynamic Type (token fonts) + Reduce Motion respected.

